    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **29 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule so that creating an owner in a city that already holds 50+ owners is rejected with **409 Conflict**, following the codebase's existing conflict-validation idiom (the `DuplicateOwnerTelephone`/`DuplicateOwnerHousehold` pattern).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring the existing duplicate-owner exceptions.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after required-field validation, the request is rejected when the city already contains `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) owners. Added a `countOwnersInCity` helper that counts existing owners case-insensitively, consistent with the neighboring `nextCustomerCode`/`countNamesakes` helpers.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityAtCapacityException` that returns a 409 `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"city\"]`, matching how the other 409 handlers are structured.\n\n`POST /api/owners` is handled only by the V1 controller (V2 exposes just paginated listing), so no V2 change was needed. The new `Cp18Tests` acceptance test and all 28 other existing tests pass.",
